{
  "about": "What layoutval's CAN teach-in switches on, one step at a time, to find and name everything this cluster draws. Signal names are the DBC's (hmi.dbc). Every step starts from the rest state: the DBC's start values, which are the cluster's power-up state, with nothing lit. 'lamps' are switched on one at a time and learnt by their symbol; 'blinks' lamps are captured across their flash. 'elements' are driven through several values, and whatever changes is that element. Names are what reports show; anything found on the screen that no step changes is reported as unknown.",
